            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A computer-implemented method for controlling the operation of at least one robotic system, the method comprising: receiving state information from at least one robotic system in an environment, the state information created by the at least one robotic system; processing the state information to generate a virtual robotic system model of at least part of the at least one robotic system in the environment; causing a visualisation of the virtual robotic system model to be displayed to at least one user; receiving a user instruction for performing an operation while the visualisation is being displayed to the at least one user; and issuing a command based on the received user instruction to the at least one robotic system to cause the at least one robotic system to perform the operation.</p>
            </abstract>
